From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:08:22 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 003/230] UX truth pass: real rating histograms, out-of-page
 rank, player-name summaries, localized errors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Rating distribution comes from the server (GROUP BY over crowd_ratings,
  10 integer buckets per player) instead of the client's single-bucket
  approximation — RateSheet now renders the real histogram
- Leaderboards: server-computed viewer rank with the board's own tiebreak
  surfaces as a 'you' row when it sits below the top-100 page
- Prediction summaries show localized player names (cache-hit on the
  lineups query), not raw ESPN ids
- ErrorBoundary copy localized EN/FA; bot /start and /myteams reply in the
  recipient's stored app language via server/messages.ts
- Ratings rows carry the match's real competition instead of defaulting to
  PL (MatchDetail + Ratings page)
- eslint ignores dist-server (stale build output was polluting lint)

